        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "ac46ff83-309c-3aa3-823f-e81a6b905c87",
                "word": "essentialisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9e5cd91e-2d87-452b-854c-476ce44d66c2",
                        "entry_id": "ac46ff83-309c-3aa3-823f-e81a6b905c87",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "essentialismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb97dffb-c00d-3f4f-ac92-a307d534cd0d",
                        "entry_id": "ac46ff83-309c-3aa3-823f-e81a6b905c87",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Doctrine qui s’attache à l’étude de l’essence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae0261e0-fdd8-4bfe-b4d9-a06ff0cf2115",
                                "sense_id": "eb97dffb-c00d-3f4f-ac92-a307d534cd0d",
                                "text": "Le monde qu’on m’enseignait se disposait harmonieusement autour de coordonnées fixes et de catégories tranchées. Les notions neutres en avaient été bannies : pas de milieu entre le traître et le héros, le renégat et le martyr ; tout fruit non comestible était vénéneux ; on m’assurait que « j’aimais » tous les membres de ma famille, y compris mes grand-tantes les plus disgraciées. Dès mes premiers balbutiements, mon expérience démentit cet essentialisme."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a47a96fa-6ff7-3c4e-8f8c-4cc61c65b300",
                        "entry_id": "ac46ff83-309c-3aa3-823f-e81a6b905c87",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Conception selon laquelle les diverses espèces animales et végétales diffèrent entre elles par essence, ce qui implique la reconnaissance de la discontinuité du vivant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a75b0639-fe24-3ba6-a77e-c0dda928a247",
                        "entry_id": "ac46ff83-309c-3aa3-823f-e81a6b905c87",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Conception selon laquelle les diverses ethnies et leurs identités socioculturelles diffèreraient entre elles par essence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "43ec8b47-4013-3b97-86fc-77bbb1839fb0",
                        "entry_id": "ac46ff83-309c-3aa3-823f-e81a6b905c87",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Conception selon laquelle, en raison d'un déterminisme biologique, les hommes et les femmes ou d'autres groupes ont par nature des caractéristiques, des aptitudes, des rôles sociaux distincts et immuables."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10d01a72-71ac-4a7d-a1fc-10092d094dbf",
                                "sense_id": "43ec8b47-4013-3b97-86fc-77bbb1839fb0",
                                "text": "Les analyses féministes ont largement critiqué l’essentialisme car il favorise l’émergence de discours enfermant les femmes dans leurs corps (dans leurs caractéristiques anatomiques, biologiques et dans leur fonction reproductrice)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c405ddd-f64e-42e9-ba72-89e4833314a6",
                                "sense_id": "43ec8b47-4013-3b97-86fc-77bbb1839fb0",
                                "text": "Sur la question du féminisme, le différentialisme revient à un essentialisme, puisqu'il insiste sur des différences de nature (d'essence) entre hommes et femmes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "765718c0-9d06-475b-aaf5-2f59de548440",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac46ff83-309c-3aa3-823f-e81a6b905c87",
                        "target_lang_word": "Essentialismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Essentialismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa0489dd-c33e-3f76-b435-99c7f7764bef",
                                        "entry_id": "191642d5-035f-35a1-82ba-73623e84f472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lehre, die der Sache nach bis auf die griechischen Philosophen Platon und Aristoteles zurückgeht und den Grund und das Wesentliche aller Dinge in ihrer Wesensform, ihrer sogenannten Essenz und nicht in ihrem Stoff oder ihrer Existenz sieht"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4421e7db-23f1-40be-b32f-45a54a0c95b5",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0489dd-c33e-3f76-b435-99c7f7764bef",
                                                "text": "Der Existentialismus formuliert gegen den Essentialismus die Priorität der Existenz vor der Essenz."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c5def31-256a-419d-abc8-98b88c14b5b8",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0489dd-c33e-3f76-b435-99c7f7764bef",
                                                "text": "Der französische Philosoph Étienne Gilson sieht die gesamte abendländische Philosophie bis zu Hegel durch einen Essentialismus geprägt mit Ausnahme der Philosophie des Thomas von Aquin."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2b5d81ae-4b28-41c9-9338-37bdb1d70881",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac46ff83-309c-3aa3-823f-e81a6b905c87",
                        "target_lang_word": "essentialism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "essentialism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2cdecdd-518f-3055-9da8-b90ea14fef7d",
                                        "entry_id": "8e78ab5a-8f9e-3205-9673-b3a27604940d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The view that objects have properties that are essential to them."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb8fec0b-57c8-4f0f-9282-bc4f3083a332",
                                                "sense_id": "f2cdecdd-518f-3055-9da8-b90ea14fef7d",
                                                "text": "More problematic is the essentialism that interests modal logicians, namely \"the view that some attributes belong to an object by necessity whereas others belong to it contingently.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0287ece-a07e-4850-9f18-5e7a6f92757c",
                                                "sense_id": "f2cdecdd-518f-3055-9da8-b90ea14fef7d",
                                                "text": "Opponents of essentialism argue that \"essences\" are simply creations of language and culture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f7ae03c9-61d9-321f-8ec5-8037bfa4a469",
                                        "entry_id": "8e78ab5a-8f9e-3205-9673-b3a27604940d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The view that all members of certain groups of people (such as those with the same race, gender, age, or sexual orientation) have common, essential traits inherent to the defining feature of the group; (also) behavior or statement(s) that reflect such a view."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ca3b48f-9310-4460-aac4-a792c26d1f40",
                                                "sense_id": "f7ae03c9-61d9-321f-8ec5-8037bfa4a469",
                                                "text": "A closer examination of the components of essentialism is required for a better understanding of the relation between essentialism and prejudice toward the two social categories of interest in this dissertation, African Americans and gay men."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47761ba1-093f-4cb5-81fe-6663d32c64f4",
                                                "sense_id": "f7ae03c9-61d9-321f-8ec5-8037bfa4a469",
                                                "text": "Like most of those who use the term, I continue to think essentialism a bad thing, but what exactly is wrong with it? Is it a matter of degree, a question of context or something that must be avoided at all costs?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd4b4d98-b310-4f31-a7cd-f68399559d63",
                                                "sense_id": "f7ae03c9-61d9-321f-8ec5-8037bfa4a469",
                                                "text": "I think we need to sophisticate our understanding of cultural essentialisms, including gender ones, because it might help us deal better with issues of resistance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68711e20-20ba-4aa8-84de-bdb94e4d430d",
                                                "sense_id": "f7ae03c9-61d9-321f-8ec5-8037bfa4a469",
                                                "text": "Colonial discourse relied heavily on such essentialisms wherein a race or ethnic group was first represented as possessing certain key features and then those very features were 'applied' to all members of the group."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec6fdeba-9cd7-4f93-82a9-fc3e36b54718",
                                                "sense_id": "f7ae03c9-61d9-321f-8ec5-8037bfa4a469",
                                                "text": "Previous literature tracks the trajectory of gender theories from biological essentialism to social construction."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f68da22a-a02e-4cf6-9549-f0c7c4478c76",
                                                "sense_id": "f7ae03c9-61d9-321f-8ec5-8037bfa4a469",
                                                "text": "The appearance underlines past incidents in which Pinker has encountered criticism for his association with advocates of so-called “human biodiversity”, which other academics have called a “rebranding” of racial genetic essentialism and scientific racism."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "234f2c5b-162c-3cc3-8c1d-9b3c436a9c59",
                                        "entry_id": "8e78ab5a-8f9e-3205-9673-b3a27604940d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The doctrine that there are certain traditional concepts, values, and skills that are essential to society and should be taught to all students."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b9e203a-88ef-49f6-a3fc-d296750319a1",
                                                "sense_id": "234f2c5b-162c-3cc3-8c1d-9b3c436a9c59",
                                                "text": "If a curriculum is dedicated to getting back to the basics, then we can be sure that the guiding philosophy is that of essentialism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6d1f51a-2735-4483-8c5b-aa77862ddb19",
                                                "sense_id": "234f2c5b-162c-3cc3-8c1d-9b3c436a9c59",
                                                "text": "Arguments of “back to basics” are usually associated with essentialism, and many contemporary educational theorists still suggest that the “nonessentials” should be taken out of the school curriculum."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8ff47f87-b613-3b71-8a0a-320e23476b05",
                                        "entry_id": "8e78ab5a-8f9e-3205-9673-b3a27604940d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lifestyle that seeks to minimize nonessentials in order to focus on what is important."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4aa7cf3f-7659-4b50-8c82-ff01142d1ad1",
                                                "sense_id": "8ff47f87-b613-3b71-8a0a-320e23476b05",
                                                "text": "In this example is the basic value proposition of Essentialism: only once you give yourself permission to stop trying to do it all, to stop saying yes to everyone, can you make your highest contribution towards the things that really matter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbfa961e-6859-42dd-984d-e26954202c48",
                                                "sense_id": "8ff47f87-b613-3b71-8a0a-320e23476b05",
                                                "text": "As a brand, ETQ is built around a philosophy which is entirely dedicated to essentialism. Everything from the creation of the label to the design of each product is inspired by three principles: simplicity, timelessness and quality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ad999ab-1346-395e-859f-895591cbd804",
                                        "entry_id": "8e78ab5a-8f9e-3205-9673-b3a27604940d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The theory that human beings are by nature (i.e. essentially) good and that evil is the product of society."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e346cc43-86a7-47d0-9e5e-63fcb270ea31",
                                                "sense_id": "6ad999ab-1346-395e-859f-895591cbd804",
                                                "text": "I should also mention that Rousseau's essentialism, unlike many of his contemporaries', is rather limited."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d845961c-42ad-4393-b8d3-8d3694d8b340",
                                                "sense_id": "6ad999ab-1346-395e-859f-895591cbd804",
                                                "text": "But they fed what they saw as raw, unguarded essentialism into work that was anything but naive. Rousseau was a naïf himself; his work as seductively strange to the other modernists as an ancient Iberian sculpture or a child’s drawing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "be6e7bd0-7f3b-4914-a153-319a3d738db0",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac46ff83-309c-3aa3-823f-e81a6b905c87",
